  steps: [
    { math: '1 · The two axes', note: 'Economic (left: redistribute; right: market) and social (liberal: individual freedom; conservative: tradition/order). The grid explains why "left" and "right" alone mislead — a libertarian and a socialist can agree on social freedom and split on economics.' },
    { math: '2 · Liberalism', note: 'Core: individual rights, rule of law, markets, tolerance. From Locke to Mill to Rawls. Its internal split: classical (minimal state) vs social (welfare state corrects market outcomes).' },
